 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "It may be that purer minds now awake\nThan were before our ancient age:\nThat the tongue's keen glances never,\nAs on the barbed moods they fire,\nMay thus have dawned upon thy face, Lady,\nAnd yet their clearest meaning,\nIn thy wild and waning rage unknown,\nShall have found its owner in thee. Lady,\nLook forth from this nightingale's nest;\nThere hearken to his lovely cryes; behold\nHis eyes by some weary hour\nGrew like her slumberous eyes.",
